---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Why Cytidel"
  description="The work your team did manually three years ago doesn't scale to the world they're operating in now. Cytidel is the early warning layer for security teams who already know this — and need to operate accordingly."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h1">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <h1 id="hero-h1">A scaling problem needs a <span class="hi-deep">scalable</span> answer</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">The work your team did manually three years ago doesn't scale to the world they're operating in now.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a href="/book-a-demo" class="btn btn-primary" data-analytics="CTA|Book a Demo|Hero">
            Book a Demo
            <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="awards-strip" aria-label="Awards and recognition">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="awards-band">
        <div class="awards-grid">
          <div class="award-item">
            <span class="award-status">
              <svg class="award-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7 4h10v5a5 5 0 0 1-10 0V4z"/>
                <path d="M7 6H4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 2.5 4.5M17 6h2.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 4.5"/>
                <path d="M12 14v3M8.5 21h7M9.5 21a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0"/>
              </svg>
              Grand Prix Winner
            </span>
            <div class="award-name">Irish National Startup of the Year, 2024</div>
          </div>
          <div class="award-item">
            <span class="award-status">
              <svg class="award-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7 4h10v5a5 5 0 0 1-10 0V4z"/>
                <path d="M7 6H4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 2.5 4.5M17 6h2.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 4.5"/>
                <path d="M12 14v3M8.5 21h7M9.5 21a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0"/>
              </svg>
              Finalist
            </span>
            <div class="award-name">Cyber Startup Award, Infosecurity Europe 2026</div>
          </div>
          <div class="award-item">
            <span class="award-status">
              <svg class="award-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7 4h10v5a5 5 0 0 1-10 0V4z"/>
                <path d="M7 6H4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 2.5 4.5M17 6h2.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 4.5"/>
                <path d="M12 14v3M8.5 21h7M9.5 21a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0"/>
              </svg>
              Finalist
            </span>
            <div class="award-name">ECSO CISO Choice Award, 2026</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="morning" aria-labelledby="morning-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="morning-h2">A typical morning</h2>
      <div class="morning-grid">
        <div class="morning-stats">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="big">300–400</span>
            <p>vulnerabilities cross your team's desk every day.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="big">Hundreds</span>
            <p>of suppliers and software components to monitor — continuously, not annually.</p>
          </div>
          <blockquote class="morning-pull">"The workload doubles every two years. The threat landscape is accelerating. Your team hasn't."</blockquote>
        </div>
        <div class="morning-help">
          <h3>How Cytidel helps</h3>
          <p>Cytidel processes all of them — and shows you the two or three that actually matter, with the evidence, the threat actor context, and the exploitation signals behind every call.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="changed" aria-labelledby="changed-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="changed-h2">What's changed</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">The world your programme was built for doesn't exist anymore.</p>

      <div class="changed-grid">
        <article class="changed-card span-2">
          <h3>Catalogues can't keep up</h3>
          <p>Vulnerabilities are discovered faster than the official catalogues can track. The work was built for a publication rhythm that doesn't exist anymore.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="changed-card dark">
          <h3>Time-to-exploit has collapsed</h3>
          <p>Weaponised in hours — sometimes minutes — of disclosure. Your scanner runs on a cycle; your team works in days.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="changed-card">
          <h3>The board is at the table</h3>
          <p>Every breach in the news and every supplier failure puts the question back on them: are we at risk?</p>
        </article>
        <article class="changed-card span-2">
          <h3>The CISO has to translate</h3>
          <p>Threat actor activity, turned into board-ready intelligence: who's active in our industry, what they're using, where we stand. The team with the evidence ready wins that conversation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="changed-card dark regulator span-3">
          <div>
            <h3>The regulator wants evidence</h3>
            <p>NIS2 and DORA made supplier and software monitoring a board-level obligation. The question isn't whether you knew — it's whether you could have known.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reg-pills"><span class="reg-pill">NIS2</span><span class="reg-pill">DORA</span></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="gaps" aria-labelledby="gaps-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="gaps-h2">Where the gaps live</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Put those shifts together and they land in one place: the distance between what's already happening and what your team can see in time.</p>

      <div class="gap-cards">
        <article class="gap-card">
          <h3>The speed gap</h3>
          <p>The threat landscape moves in hours. Your scanner runs on a cycle. By the time you've connected the dots, the attacker has already moved.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gap-card">
          <h3>The visibility gap</h3>
          <p>Nobody is watching when a vendor in your stack gets breached at 2am. You watch the headlines and hope the things you miss aren't the ones that matter.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gap-card">
          <h3>The context gap</h3>
          <p>CVSS measures theoretical severity, not real-world risk. 30% of CVEs linked to known threat actors in 2025 were rated Low or Medium.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="gaps-answer">The answer isn't more people responding faster. It's defenders moving at <span>computer&nbsp;speed.</span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="built-for" aria-labelledby="built-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="built-for-card">
        <h2 id="built-h2">What Cytidel is built for</h2>
        <p class="opener">Cytidel is the early warning layer for vulnerabilities, threat actors and supplier risk. Not a replacement for your scanner. Not a replacement for your CTI feeds. The layer that ties them together and makes their output actionable in real time.</p>

        <div class="principles">
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="yes">Threat-led prioritisation</span>
            <span class="no">not score-led.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="yes">Real-time intelligence</span>
            <span class="no">not weekly digests.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="yes">Evidence behind every decision</span>
            <span class="no">not gut feel.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="principle">
            <span class="yes">Continuous monitoring across your stack and your suppliers</span>
            <span class="no">not annual reviews.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="closer">Threats don't wait for your scan cycle. Threat actors don't pick by score. Boards don't ask about CVSS averages. Cytidel exists for the security teams who've already realised this — and need to operate accordingly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="heading-sec" aria-labelledby="heading-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="heading-grid">
        <div class="heading-intro">
          <h2 id="heading-h2">Where this is heading</h2>
          <p>Surfacing the signal earlier and earlier, before the threats that matter have a chance to land. We're investing heavily in predictive intelligence to get there.</p>
          <div class="methodology-card">
            <h4>The methodology works</h4>
            <p>Cytidel's predictive flagging on vulnerabilities that later show real exploitation signals — proof-of-concept, exploit availability, or threat actor association.</p>
            <div class="methodology-stat">
              <span class="num">~70%</span>
              <span class="label">Flagged early,<br/>exploited later</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="roadmap-list">
          <article class="roadmap-card">
            <h3>Spotlight Integration</h3>
            <p>The first version of our predictive capability. Across the three years we've run Spotlight, we've flagged under 1% of all new vulnerabilities — the few that genuinely warrant early attention.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="roadmap-card">
            <h3>Machine Learning Scale</h3>
            <p>Scaling the analytical approach with machine learning, built on years of vulnerability events, threat actor activity, exploit signals, and supplier intelligence.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="roadmap-card">
            <h3>Continuous Intelligence</h3>
            <p>More depth, more coverage, faster response to the threats that matter — and fewer missed because the team didn't see them in time. Shipped capability today; the same foundations underneath what's next.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="final-cta-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="final-cta-card">
        <h2 id="final-cta-h2">Ready to see Cytidel?</h2>
        <p>Meet with a Cytidel expert to discuss how you can get ahead of emerging threats, understand the latest threat actor activity relevant to your business, and monitor critical software and suppliers 24/7.</p>
        <a href="/book-a-demo" class="btn btn-primary" data-analytics="CTA|Book a Demo|Final CTA">
          Book a Demo
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Container + section defaults */
  .container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-left: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
    padding-right: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
  }
  section {
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px);
  }

  /* Shared heading baseline (heroh1 + section h2/h3) */
  .hero h1,
  .morning h2,
  .changed h2,
  .gaps h2,
  .built-for-card h2,
  .heading-intro h2,
  .final-cta-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.6vw, 4.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .morning h2,
  .changed h2,
  .gaps h2,
  .built-for-card h2,
  .heading-intro h2,
  .final-cta-card h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
  }

  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(80px, 12vw, 160px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(24px, 3.5vw, 44px);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: -200px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 1200px;
    height: 800px;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(128, 252, 19, 0.08) 0%, transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .hi-deep { color: var(--color-accent-deep); }
  .hero-sub {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.7vw, 1.32rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  .hero-cta { margin-top: 40px; }

  /* Awards strip */
  .awards-strip {
    padding-top: clamp(4px, 1vw, 10px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 32px);
  }
  .awards-band {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f2823 0%, #0e1612 100%);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: clamp(13px, 1.6vw, 18px) clamp(20px, 2.8vw, 40px);
  }
  .awards-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
  }
  .award-item {
    padding: 0 clamp(12px, 1.8vw, 22px);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .award-item:first-child { border-left: none; padding-left: 0; }
  .award-item:last-child { padding-right: 0; }
  .award-status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .award-icon { width: 14px; height: 14px; color: var(--color-accent); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .award-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(0.78rem, 1vw, 0.9rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .awards-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; }
    .award-item { border-left: none; padding: 0; }
    .award-item + .award-item {
      padding-top: 14px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border);
    }
  }

  /* Section 2 — A typical morning */
  .morning h2 { margin-bottom: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .morning-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 28px);
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .morning-stats {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(16px, 2vw, 20px);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .stat-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 12px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  .stat-card .big {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .stat-card p {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.1rem);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .morning-pull {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.8vw, 1.45rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding-left: clamp(20px, 3vw, 28px);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .morning-help {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f2823 0%, var(--color-dark-bg) 100%);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px);
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .morning-help h3 {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.4vw, 1.9rem);
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .morning-help p {
    color: var(--color-dark-text-secondary);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.18rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .morning-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* Section 3 — What's changed (bento) */
  .changed { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .changed h2 { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .section-lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.55vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 clamp(40px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
  .changed-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px);
  }
  .changed-card {
    padding: clamp(28px, 3vw, 36px);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .changed-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 1.7vw, 1.4rem);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .changed-card p {
    font-size: clamp(0.96rem, 1.35vw, 1.04rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .changed-card.span-2 { grid-column: span 2; }
  .changed-card.span-3 { grid-column: span 3; }
  .changed-card.dark {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f2823 0%, var(--color-dark-bg) 100%);
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
  }
  .changed-card.dark h3 { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .changed-card.dark p { color: var(--color-dark-text-secondary); }
  .changed-card.regulator {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .changed-card.regulator > div {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 280px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .reg-pills { display: flex; gap: 12px; }
  .reg-pill {
    padding: 10px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .changed-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .changed-card.span-2, .changed-card.span-3 { grid-column: span 1; }
    .changed-card.regulator { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }

  /* Section 4 — Where the gaps live */
  .gaps { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .gaps h2 { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .gap-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 28px);
  }
  .gap-card {
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .gap-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.7vw, 1.32rem);
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .gap-card p {
    font-size: clamp(0.96rem, 1.35vw, 1.02rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .gap-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .gaps-answer {
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 60px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .gaps-answer span {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Section 5 — What Cytidel is built for (dark card) */
  .built-for { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .built-for-card {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f2823 0%, var(--color-dark-bg) 100%);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(40px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
  }
  .built-for-card h2 {
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
    margin-bottom: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  .built-for-card .opener,
  .built-for-card .closer {
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-dark-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(14px, 1.8vw, 20px);
    margin: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px) 0;
  }
  .principle {
    padding: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    background: #eceee8;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .principle .yes {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .principle .no {
    font-size: clamp(0.85rem, 1.2vw, 0.92rem);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .principles { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .principles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* Section 6 — Where this is heading */
  .heading-sec { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .heading-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 3fr;
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px);
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .heading-intro h2 { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .heading-intro > p {
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px);
  }
  .methodology-card {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1f2823 0%, var(--color-dark-bg) 100%);
    color: var(--color-dark-text);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: clamp(26px, 3vw, 34px);
  }
  .methodology-card h4 {
